From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Shader set: records layout 2, each program's code stored once; the records are rebuilt as they are read

T108 and T109 (batches t108-s, t109-s): the conversion of Ocarina's full set is 67 minutes, all of
it the console writing prep_shader_set.bin: 113,054 records, 4,311 MB, at 1 to 1.5 MB a second
after the first half GB, whatever the size of the write calls (0527). The file repeats the
lowered code of a program in every record that uses it: 36,542 programs for 113,054 records.

Layout 2 writes a record as its fact ids and its key, then each used fact once and each used
program's lowered code once, then a trailer that says where those parts are. ShaderSet::ReadRecords
builds a record's environments again from those parts and hands them to the same callback the
preparation gave VideoCommon::ReadPipelines (FileEnvironment::Deserialize and the key read only
forward, so each record is read from memory through an ifstream with its buffer swapped). A stamp
of the old layout does not hold ('records layout 2' is a stamp line), so a console with an old
set converts once more.

Not compiled before this build; nothing changes without EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET.

